  NOTE (stated before the numbers): the primary outer-slope estimator a2 comes from a fit to the DARK MASS alone and never uses a0, so it is identical on the two footings BY CONSTRUCTION -- the footings differ only in where they put r_M.
  10/12 clusters have a usable r_M. A1644, A2255 have max(g/a0) = 0.95, 0.97 < 1 over the whole profile: they never reach the Newtonian regime, so on the framework's own criterion their entire measured profile is beyond the break (their outer window therefore starts at 60 kpc).
